+++ b/docs/retained-instances.md
@@ -0,0 +1,63 @@
+# Retained instance packets
+
+Frames may enable a retained set of unskinned instances using
+`retained_enabled`, `retained_reset`, `instances` upserts and `instance_removals`.
+The generated Instance carries `id_low`, `id_high`, `order`, mesh, material,
+transform and optional four-lane parameters. IDs comprise two exact 16-bit
+lanes; order is at most 16777215. Retained instances follow immediate draws,
+sorted by `(order, id)`. Immediate pose indices remain unchanged. Extra vec4s,
+skinning and per-view visibility remain immediate-draw features.
+
+A fresh program must send reset before any deltas. Create, restore, reload and
+unaccepted validation after time travel start a fresh retained epoch. A reset
+replaces the set; a disabled frame clears it and must carry no retained changes.
+Duplicate IDs, including remove plus upsert of the same ID, reject the frame.
+Removing an unknown ID is idempotent. Immediate plus retained draws cannot
+exceed MAX_DRAWS. The packet decoder validates finite matrices, bounded IDs,
+parameters and catalog references.
+
+GameRuntime materializes a candidate view, validates it through the host and
+commits retained changes with the accepted guest frame. Invalid or rejected
+frames preserve accepted instance state. Old RenderFrame values own their draw
+arrays. Front ends using GameRuntime receive the same ordinary full draw list;
+custom decoder consumers can use `pen_runtime::instances::Instances` explicitly.
+Raw packet recordings must retain reset packets and replay all deltas in order.
+
+The existing renderer keeps GPU instance contents and uploads changed ranges.
+This protocol avoids serializing and decoding unchanged matrices; it does not
+remove CPU traversal, sorting or view assembly. Dynamic visibility changes need
+upserts/removals, or immediate draws for view-dependent objects. Reordering can
+increase GPU upload work. Applications own stable identities, dirty sets and
+reset policy; none is inferred from game state by Pen.
+
+Generate with `just sync-protocol`. The lightweight equivalent is
+`just gdev=PROJECT pen='cargo run -q -p pen-codegen --example generate --' sync-protocol`.
+The example invokes the same generator without building a desktop host.
+
+`cargo run --release -p pen-runtime --example instances` compares actual packet
+decode and view assembly for 4096 instances, 16 frames, 1% dirty, including the
+cold retained reset. On 2026-10-23, immediate took 1.4615 ms versus retained
+2.0835 ms for all 16 frames; packet bytes fell from 6301056 to 497984. These CPU
+timings exclude guest encoding, rendering and initial packet construction. Ink's
+paired guest measurement separately reduced encoding from 19.19 to 5.18 ms.
+The host assembly overhead is a remaining optimization opportunity.
+
+Headless verification includes generated schema freshness, protocol framing and
+malformed data, runtime accepted/rejected frames, full U32 IDs, deterministic
+ordering, reset/remove/reorder, old snapshots and the existing upload planner.
+No window or GPU timing is needed for the protocol benchmark.
+
+Accepted updates cache their sorted draw view and ID-to-slot map. A delta with
+unchanged membership/order copies this view and patches changed slots; structural
+changes rebuild it. Earlier frames remain independent, and rejected candidates
+never advance the cache or its revision.
+
+The resolved frame carries host-only `DrawChanges`: the before/after revision
+identities, the first retained slot after immediate draws, and sorted absolute
+dirty draw indices. This metadata is not serialized. Hosts editing resolved
+draws independently must clear it. The renderer trusts only a connected revision
+chain with unchanged retained ordering; skipped frames, reset or reordering use
+bitwise value comparison. Culling/LOD placement and default material parameters
+are also checked per GPU slot. The CPU instance buffer is the GPU shadow; no
+second full copy is required. Sparse dirty ranges are coalesced with a bounded
+write count, and a replaced GPU buffer receives a complete upload.
